-- Regression: RRB.push (Array.push's PVec/TrieNode/List(a) trie, specialised
-- to Float) crashed compiled on the SECOND push, well before the tail buffer
-- (32 elements) or trie levels are involved.
--
-- Array.push calls `lst_len(tail)` to measure the tail buffer.  lst_len's
-- inner `go` discards the list-head field via a wildcard pattern
-- (`Cons(_, t) -> go(t, acc + 1)`).  The pattern-matrix compiler
-- (lower_match.ml) gives EVERY constructor-field synthetic variable the
-- `TVar "_"` placeholder type at creation; a NAMED field (`Cons(h, t)`) gets
-- fixed up to its real, trackable type when re-bound via `ty_of_span`, and
-- that real type then flows through mono.ml's monomorphization substitution
-- normally — but a WILDCARD-discarded field is never rebound, so it keeps
-- `TVar "_"` forever. `Rc_types.needs_rc (TVar "_")` conservatively answers
-- true ("assume heap-carrying"), so Perceus emits a `dec_rc` on the discarded
-- field. For a concretely-Float instantiation, the field's actual runtime
-- representation is a raw unboxed IEEE-754 double bit-reinterpreted as `ptr`
-- (`Llvm_ctx.coerce ("double","ptr")` — a plain bitcast, no heap box), so
-- that `dec_rc` reads the tag field out of a raw float bit pattern and
-- SIGSEGVs (`march_decrc + 52`, faulting address `0x3ff8...0008`).
--
-- Fixed by recording PatWild's inferred type into typecheck.ml's `type_map`
-- (mirroring PatVar) and having lower_match.ml's pattern-matrix compiler look
-- up EVERY constructor field's type via `ty_of_span` instead of defaulting
-- unconditionally to the unknown-type placeholder — so a discarded field now
-- flows through monomorphization exactly like a named one.
mod Main do
  needs IO.Console
  fn main(_cap_console : Cap(IO.Console)) do
    let v0 = RRB.empty()
    let v1 = RRB.push(v0, 1.5)
    let v2 = RRB.push(v1, 2.5)
    let v3 = RRB.push(v2, 3.5)
    println(RRB.length(v3))
  end
end
